1.  Remember that > 0 is exclusive of zero, and that >= 0 is inclusive of zero.



2.  The if statement is designed to verify a boolean condition. If the condition evaluates to true, the code within the block is executed; otherwise, it's not executed.



  if (true) {
      // code inside this block will be executed
  }

  if (false) {
      // code inside this block will NOT be executed
  }